course: dictionary
lesson: 14525
title: Permeate: spreading through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To permeate means to spread through every part of something, reaching into all the corners. Look at the clue in this sentence: «The smell of bread permeated the house.» The smell did not stay in the kitchen. It reached every room, so permeated must mean spread through.
explain: The same word is used in science. Water can permeate soil by moving through the tiny gaps between the grains. «Water permeates the soil.» A rock that lets water through is permeable, and a rock that does not is impermeable. The prefix im- means not, just as in impossible.
explain: In stories, permeate often describes feelings or ideas, not only smells or liquids. «Fear permeated the village.» The fear did not stay in one house. It spread through the whole village. Permeate is a formal word, so you will meet it most often in books, news reports and school writing.
fact: To permeate means to spread through every part of something.
fact: «Permeated» is the past tense of permeate: «The smell of bread permeated the house.»
fact: In science, a liquid or a gas can permeate a material by passing through it.
fact: A permeable rock lets water through; an impermeable rock does not.
fact: Permeate is a formal word, so it is more common in writing than in everyday talk.
exercise: «The smell of rain permeated the whole town.» What does permeated mean? | Was forgotten | Stopped at the door | *Spread through every part | Washed away
exercise: Science: «Water slowly permeated the sandy soil.» What is the water doing? | It is staying in one puddle on top | It is boiling away into the sky | *It is passing through the soil | It is turning into ice
exercise: «Fear permeated the village.» Find and copy the word that means spread through. | *permeated | Fear | the | village
test: Which rock lets water through? | Impermeable rock | Metal | *Permeable rock | Glass
test: «The music permeated every room in the house.» Which word means nearly the same as permeated? | *Spread through | Avoided | Ignored
exam: «A gas can permeate a cloth.» What does permeate mean here? | Freeze solid | Sit on top | *Pass through or spread through | Change colour
